INT. TERRAFORMING STATION DOME - CONTROL DECK - DAY

A broad glass cupola overlooks a rust-red landscape speckled with the first green. Atmospheric processors the size of cathedrals churn on the horizon. Inside, a ring of consoles, each glowing in a different color.

Six people work the ring.

ADMIRAL SELENE VOSKUIJLEN-ADEYEMI (60s, silver crop, high collar) paces the center. COMMANDER RAMIRO OKONJO-TALLIS (40s, shaved head, burn scar on one cheek) taps at a console. DOCTOR YUKI HARTMANN-NWAFOR (30s, braids, lab coat) studies a spectrograph. ENGINEER BODHI LARSSON-EZE (20s, sleeveless jacket, goggles on his forehead) crouches under a panel. LIEUTENANT CASSANDRA MBEKI-FROST (30s, tight bun) monitors a bank of weather maps. And last, at a small console apart from the others, THE OBSERVER, an elderly man known only by his badge, watches without touching anything.

SELENE
Report.

RAMIRO
Oxygen at eleven percent.

YUKI
Methane trace is falling.

BODHI
(from under the panel)
Pump six is slow.

CASSANDRA
Storm cell northeast. Forty minutes out.

SELENE
Can the dome hold?

BODHI
It's held worse.

SELENE
That is not an answer.

BODHI
(emerging)
Yes, Admiral.

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over the speaker, filtered)
Station, this is Earth Control. Please confirm your count.

SELENE
Control, we confirm six souls.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Six. Understood. Be advised, the board has questions about the Observer.

The Observer's head turns. Nobody else moves.

SELENE
(to the speaker)
Control, he has all clearances.

CONTROL (V.O.)
It's not about clearances.

SELENE
Then what is it about?

A long silence. Static.

CONTROL (V.O.)
He was registered dead in 2091.

Every head turns toward the Observer. He smiles, an old, courteous smile, and stands, smoothing his badge.

THE OBSERVER
It was a clerical error.

SELENE
(softly)
Of course it was.

Ramiro rises. Cassandra rises. Yuki drops her pen. Bodhi steps out from the panel and wipes his hands, slowly, on his trousers.

THE OBSERVER
I am sorry to have worried you. I am here only to watch.

SELENE
Watch what?

THE OBSERVER
The part that comes after you.

Outside, the first thin line of storm cloud crosses the red horizon.
